    "summary": "Spring ’90 high‑energy show featuring epic Blow Away solo & perfect China Cat → Rider",
    "blurb": "The Knick run delivers a blazing first set with Hell In A Bucket, Dupree’s Diamond Blues and a fire‑filled Blow Away. The second set shines with the classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and a soaring Morning Dew into Brokedown Palace encore. Brent Mydland’s keyboards are magical throughout.",
    "review": "On March 26, 1990 at Albany’s Knickerbocker Arena the Dead turned in one of the spring‑90 era’s most electrifying performances. The first set roared to life with a thunderous Hell In A Bucket, a ripping Dupree’s Diamond Blues and a jaw‑dropping Blow Away solo that several fans called “the best ever.” Brent Mydland was in top form, laying down tight, soaring keyboards on Blow Away and weaving his signature 1990 MIDI solo into the mix. \n\nThe second set kept the momentum rolling: Victim Or The Crime segued flawlessly into a blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that crackled with Jerry’s crystal‑clear tone, followed by a powerful Man Smart, Woman Smarter and a tight Drums/Space stretch. A triumphant I Need A Miracle led straight into Dear Mr. Fantasy, Gimme Some Lovin’ and an uplifting Morning Dew that built into a heartfelt Brokedown Palace encore. Across audience FM broadcasts, matrix feeds and several soundboard sources the show is praised for its high‑octane energy, immaculate set flow, and especially Brent’s magical keyboards and Jerry’s soaring lead work.",
